- Implement update and migration routines for database/schema changes.
- Clean up options, custom tables, and scheduled events on plugin deactivation/uninstall.
- Use `register_deactivation_hook` and `register_uninstall_hook`.
- Display admin notices using the WordPress admin notice API.
- Ensure backward compatibility for existing users.

## Examples

```php
// Register deactivation and uninstall hooks
register_deactivation_hook( __FILE__, 'my_plugin_deactivate' );
register_uninstall_hook( __FILE__, 'my_plugin_uninstall' );

function my_plugin_deactivate() {
    // Clean up scheduled events
    wp_clear_scheduled_hook( 'my_plugin_cron_event' );
}
function my_plugin_uninstall() {
    // Remove options and custom tables
    delete_option( 'my_plugin_option' );
    global $wpdb;
    $wpdb->query( "DROP TABLE IF EXISTS {$wpdb->prefix}my_plugin_table" );
}
```

```php
// Display admin notice
add_action( 'admin_notices', function() {
    echo '<div class="notice notice-success is-dismissible"><p>' . esc_html__( 'Settings saved.', 'my-plugin' ) . '</p></div>';
});
```

